<title>USA: S. Dakota corn harvest slowed by muddy fields.</title>
<headline>S. Dakota corn harvest slowed by muddy fields.</headline>
<dateline>PIERRE, S.D. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Muddy field conditions limited the amount of row crops harvested during the week ended Sunday, according to the the latest crop report from the South Dakota Agricultural Service.</p>
<p>&quot;Although the harvest is ahead of the five-year average of 72 percent, a late harvest in 1992 severely lowered the average completion rate,&quot; the report said.</p>
<p>Corn harvest progress was estimated at 78 percent, versus 58 percent last week.</p>
<p>The sunflower harvest increased to 95 percent complete, up from 90 percent a week earlier and the five-year average of 91 percent, according to the report.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720</p>
